{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794652246,"nonce":"rkmNbx65XMTdUAwssEQCElkhLQU=","title":"Test that API timestamp fields end in At","message":"A test in shared/ that walks the exported Zod schemas (objects, arrays, unions, intersections, tuples, nullables) and fails on any field whose schema is schemas.Timestamp and whose name doesn't end in At. The brand is type-only, but every timestamp field uses the same schemas.Timestamp value, so identity finds them. Misses types written by hand rather than from a schema (DocumentSummary in api.ts); the TypeScript compiler API (ts.createProgram + checker, looking for the Timestamp brand on every property in shared/) would catch those too, at more cost. CLAUDE.md has the convention.","files":null}]}